  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 48.5% accuracy while image (resnet50, singleprofile) is at chance level (~20.8%), establishing RNA as the dominant modality. Uncertainty: It is unclear whether the multiprofile setting with avgpool aggregation adds meaningful value over the single-profile baseline, or whether the single PCA profile already captures sufficient signal. This experiment (config_002) directly compares to config_001 with only the profile setting and aggregation changed, isolating the effect of multiprofile+avgpool on the stronger modality. It is the best next step because: (1) it targets the modality that actually carries signal, (2) it is a minimal, clean comparison that isolates one design axis, (3) the result will inform whether aggregation mechanisms are worth the added complexity before investing in multimodal fusion experiments, and (4) under a limited budget, confirming or rejecting the value of the aggregation pipeline on the dominant modality reduces uncertainty for all downstream decisions."
}

